				was 42,360,
			</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v15002065">
			</marker>
			<v n="65">
				besides their 
				<crossref let="z" cid="c15002065.129">
				</crossref>
				male and, 
				<crossref let="a" cid="c15002065.130">
				</crossref>
				female servants, of whom there were 7,337, and they had 200 male and female singers.
			</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v15002066">
			</marker>
			<v n="66">
				Their horses 
				<crossref let="b" cid="c15002066.131">
				</crossref>
				were 736,, 
				<crossref let="c" cid="c15002066.132">
				</crossref>
				their mules were 245,
				<note nid="n15002066.66">
				</note>
			</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v15002067">
			</marker>
			<v n="67">
				their camels 
				<crossref let="d" cid="c15002067.133">
				</crossref>
				were 435,, 
				<crossref let="e" cid="c15002067.134">
				</crossref>
				and their donkeys were 6,720.
			</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v15002068">
			</marker>
			<v n="68">
				Some of 
				<crossref let="f" cid="c15002068.135">
				</crossref>
				the heads, 
				<crossref let="g" cid="c15002068.136">
				</crossref>
				of families, when they came to the house of the LORD that is in Jerusalem, made freewill offerings for the house of God, to erect it on its site.
			</v>
			<marker class="begin-verse" mid="v15002069">
			</marker>
			<v n="69">
				According to 
				<crossref let="h" cid="c15002069.137">
				</crossref>
				their ability, 
				<crossref let="i" cid="c15002069.138">
				</crossref>
